{"name":"Verdigris Coloured","hex":"#62be77","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"verdigris","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A blue-green patina or rust that forms on copper-containing metals.","Copper acetate."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cover or coat with verdigris."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/verdigris"},{"term":"coloured","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["British standard spelling of colored."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative form of colored."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/coloured"}],"entries":[{"title":"Verdigris","blocks":[{"text":"Verdigris is a common name for any of a variety of somewhat toxic copper salts of acetic acid, which range in colour from green to a bluish-green depending on their chemical composition. Once used as a medicine and pharmaceutical preparation, verdigris occurs naturally, creating a patina on copper, bronze, and brass, and is the main component of a historic green pigment used for artistic purposes from antiquity until the late 20th century, including in easel painting, polychromatic sculptures, and illumination of maps. However, due to its instability, its popularity declined as other green pigments became readily available. The instability of its appearance stems from its hydration level and basicity, which change as the pigment interacts with other materials over time."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Verdigris"},{"title":"Coloureds","blocks":[{"text":"Coloured people are multiracial people in South Africa, Namibia, Botswana and to a smaller extent Zimbabwe and Zambia. Their ancestry descends from the interracial mixing that occurred between Europeans, Africans and Asians. Interracial mixing in South Africa began in the 17th century in the Dutch Cape Colony where the Dutch settlers mixed with Khoi Khoi women and female slaves from different parts of Africa and Asia, creating mixed-race children. Eventually, interracial mixing occurred throughout South Africa and the rest of Southern Africa with various other European nationals who mixed with other African tribes leading to more mixed-race people whose descendants would later be officially classified as 'Coloured' under the Population Registration Act, 1950 during Apartheid."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/Coloured-family.jpg/330px-Coloured-family.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coloureds"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/Verdigris.JPG/500px-Verdigris.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/Verdigris.JPG/1280px-Verdigris.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/Verdigris.JPG/500px-Verdigris.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Naturally occurring verdigris on exposed metal in the Prague Metro.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AVerdigris.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Last_Supper_%28by_Giotto_di_Bondone%29_-_Capella_degli_Scrovegni_%28Padova%29.jpg/250px-Last_Supper_%28by_Giotto_di_Bondone%29_-_Capella_degli_Scrovegni_%28Padova%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Last_Supper_%28by_Giotto_di_Bondone%29_-_Capella_degli_Scrovegni_%28Padova%29.jpg/500px-Last_Supper_%28by_Giotto_di_Bondone%29_-_Capella_degli_Scrovegni_%28Padova%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Last_Supper_%28by_Giotto_di_Bondone%29_-_Capella_degli_Scrovegni_%28Padova%29.jpg/250px-Last_Supper_%28by_Giot